                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "a3dab24e-edb1-39a2-8b68-7c74ef840871",
                        "entry_id": "fb19b561-c381-378e-a4db-94c26a274163",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Full of or possessing wit; wise; sensible"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "10c5fcfe-e697-4b1b-bfd0-8fb5a4253f61",
                                "sense_id": "a3dab24e-edb1-39a2-8b68-7c74ef840871",
                                "text": "'Tis passing miraculous that your dull and blind worship should so suddenly turn both sightful and witful"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "adfbfd65-58c2-4ec1-b92e-76499ad315bd",
                                "sense_id": "a3dab24e-edb1-39a2-8b68-7c74ef840871",
                                "text": "Do not directly ask him to buy. As one master salesman whom the author knows puts it, to do so is \"brutal.\" It is, to say the least, not witful, and what is not witful is not good salesmanship."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "03760821-9c4c-4c2e-aec6-5f5e596a4cbd",
                                "sense_id": "a3dab24e-edb1-39a2-8b68-7c74ef840871",
                                "text": "[…] the most witful, th-that it's hopeless I'm not witful."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "7f7aa493-ba69-4fd8-aa22-5bbc543f267a",
                                "sense_id": "a3dab24e-edb1-39a2-8b68-7c74ef840871",
                                "text": "l love you, she said. l find it splendid to have dropped you like a witful lobster into this boiling pot."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "a75374e4-8192-4517-9d22-fae75c3a1700",
                                "sense_id": "a3dab24e-edb1-39a2-8b68-7c74ef840871",
                                "text": "I AM LIKING HARRY. HIS MANIFESTATIONS ARE RED. THEY ARE WITFUL. \"Witful?\" WITFUL = FULL OF WIT? \"I see,\" Harry said. \"He thinks we're funny.\" FUNNY = FULL OF FUN? \"Not exactly,\" Norman said. \"We entities have the concept of . . .\" He trailed off. How was he going to explain \"funny\"?"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "005be2c3-cc5d-472d-b226-e5ae7dd95af5",
                                "sense_id": "a3dab24e-edb1-39a2-8b68-7c74ef840871",
                                "text": "And some fear hides beneath the guise of all things physically-affecting and effecting which we try with an enthusiasm unsurpassed and a witful dexterity unrivalled, to craft into some spurious raison d'être."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
